# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Alamut React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Package
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 to dependencies
- Used npm to install the package (matching the project's existing package manager)

### 2. Modified Files
- **app/package.json**: Added `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0` to dependencies
- **app/package-lock.json**: Updated lockfile with new dependency tree
- **app/src/App.tsx**: 
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the ErrorBoundary, after ToastHost and ConfirmHost

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart):

- Used the React-specific entry point (`@vercel/speed-insights/react`)
- Placed the SpeedInsights component at the root app level for proper tracking across all routes
- The component acts as a wrapper around the tracking script for seamless framework integration

## Testing & Verification

✅ **TypeScript type checking**: Passed without errors
✅ **Build**: Successfully compiled (3.36s)
✅ **Tests**: All 377 tests passed in 20 test files
✅ **No regressions**: Existing functionality preserved

## Next Steps

To enable Speed Insights in production:
1. Deploy to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Speed Insights)
3. After the next deployment, the tracking script will be automatically injected
4. Data collection will begin once users visit the deployed site

The tracking routes (`/_vercel/speed-insights/*`) will be automatically added upon deployment.
